You're not practicing what you're saying.

1811
01:07:44,628 --> 01:07:46,397
No, I'm just picking them.

1812
01:07:46,398 --> 01:07:47,498
It's so funny.

1813
01:07:48,268 --> 01:07:49,337
Who knows when I'll come back?

1814
01:07:49,338 --> 01:07:52,068
(They continued to pick...)

1815
01:07:52,168 --> 01:07:54,838
(the vegetables they needed for the day.)

1816
01:07:56,238 --> 01:07:58,578
- I feel rich. - I know. It's amazing.

1817
01:07:58,738 --> 01:07:59,808
This is it.

1818
01:08:00,678 --> 01:08:02,218
How much of crown daisy did you pick?

1819
01:08:02,348 --> 01:08:03,848
It looks like you picked more than a water deer would.

1820
01:08:04,118 --> 01:08:06,148
I thought he said he was picking enough for the day.

1821
01:08:08,648 --> 01:08:09,688
I wish I could pick more.

1822
01:08:10,158 --> 01:08:11,257
He wishes he could pick more?

1823
01:08:11,258 --> 01:08:12,328
Let's come back again.

1824
01:08:14,028 --> 01:08:15,187
I'll come back in April...

1825
01:08:15,188 --> 01:08:16,797
- to pick yuzu leaves. - Let's do that.

1826
01:08:16,798 --> 01:08:17,998
(Promising to come back next time, although they're disappointed)

1827
01:08:18,728 --> 01:08:19,827
Let's go back.

1828
01:08:19,828 --> 01:08:21,127
(Quickly returning)

1829
01:08:21,128 --> 01:08:23,667
It's a little embarrassing, though.

1830
01:08:23,668 --> 01:08:24,668
(Laughing)

1831
01:08:24,669 --> 01:08:26,038
It's not like we bought it.

1832
01:08:27,508 --> 01:08:28,708
Still, it's nice.

1833
01:08:28,908 --> 01:08:31,038
He seems genuinely happy.

1834
01:08:31,638 --> 01:08:32,907
Tell your aunt. She won't come back...

1835
01:08:32,908 --> 01:08:34,208
- once she goes. - It's really amazing.

1836
01:08:34,648 --> 01:08:36,378
- There were so many crown daisies. - I'll put my clothes away first.

1837
01:08:36,678 --> 01:08:37,718
She's surprised.

1838
01:08:38,018 --> 01:08:39,488
Try this.

1839
01:08:40,948 --> 01:08:42,857
(What they harvested for the day makes her jaw drop.)

1840
01:08:42,858 --> 01:08:44,788
- He harvested so much. - I know.

1841
01:08:46,888 --> 01:08:48,157
(Heading to the kitchen with the seafood...)

1842
01:08:48,158 --> 01:08:49,427
(she bought early in the morning)

1843
01:08:49,428 --> 01:08:50,898
I brought this down.

1844
01:08:51,158 --> 01:08:52,056
Well done.

1845
01:08:52,998 --> 01:08:54,467
Let's do it quickly.

1846
01:08:54,468 --> 01:08:55,798
Amazing.

1847
01:08:56,138 --> 01:08:57,898
Would you blanch spinach first?

1848
01:08:58,268 --> 01:08:59,307
I'm already boiling water.

1849
01:08:59,308 --> 01:09:00,538
(Perfectly coordinated)

1850
01:09:01,008 --> 01:09:03,838
The ones we harvested earlier are really nice.

1851
01:09:04,978 --> 01:09:06,278
Let's try making that today.

1852
01:09:06,678 --> 01:09:07,778
Siler divaricata tangpyeongchae.

1853
01:09:08,078 --> 01:09:09,217
- Tangpyeongchae? - Goodness.

1854
01:09:09,218 --> 01:09:10,448
Tangpyeongchae?

1855
01:09:10,878 --> 01:09:13,187
Usually, tangpyeongchae is made...

1856
01:09:13,188 --> 01:09:15,288
with mung bean jelly.

1857
01:09:15,548 --> 01:09:16,688
- That's the dish. - Oh, that?

1858
01:09:17,258 --> 01:09:18,587
It's a dish that originated from...

1859
01:09:18,588 --> 01:09:19,927
- That's right. - "Tangpyeongchaek."

1860
01:09:19,928 --> 01:09:21,587
It's called tangpyeongchae because there are various ingredients.

1861
01:09:21,588 --> 01:09:23,257
To gather them together and mix well.

1862
01:09:23,258 --> 01:09:25,868
"Tangpyeongchaek" means to recruit talented individuals fairly.

1863
01:09:25,998 --> 01:09:27,198
There's an even amount of various ingredients.

1864
01:09:28,098 --> 01:09:29,968
In Tongyeong, they add...

1865
01:09:30,238 --> 01:09:32,868
various seafood that goes well with siler divaricata,

1866
01:09:33,308 --> 01:09:35,908
so that the dish becomes more valuable.

1867
01:09:36,078 --> 01:09:38,578
That's the kind of dish it is.

1868
01:09:38,948 --> 01:09:41,247
Today, we're making siler divaricata tangpyeongchae...

1869
01:09:41,248 --> 01:09:43,218
and seolchi soup with seasoned vegetables.

1870
01:09:43,278 --> 01:09:44,418
- Seolchi soup? - Seolchi soup?

1871
01:09:44,878 --> 01:09:46,887
"Seolchi" means...

1872
