1911
01:11:12,868 --> 01:11:14,308
- Its taste... - It looks delicious.

1912
01:11:14,468 --> 01:11:15,938
- It's making me salivate. - I know.

1913
01:11:16,378 --> 01:11:18,077
This is the one you made last year.

1914
01:11:18,078 --> 01:11:19,308
We can scoop this.

1915
01:11:21,508 --> 01:11:22,678
- Scoop only the clear part. - Okay.

1916
01:11:23,578 --> 01:11:25,377
- Scoop it slowly. - There was soy sauce...

1917
01:11:25,378 --> 01:11:27,048
- that I made last year. - Just the clear part.

1918
01:11:27,188 --> 01:11:29,588
Does it taste more savory?

1919
01:11:29,988 --> 01:11:31,788
Totally. It's like a combination...

1920
01:11:32,018 --> 01:11:33,988
of fish sauce and soy sauce.

1921
01:11:35,028 --> 01:11:36,728
- This much? - Yes, that much is good.

1922
01:11:36,928 --> 01:11:38,128
Let's bring it down.

1923
01:11:38,928 --> 01:11:39,928
(Taking only enough for cooking and heading back to the kitchen)

1924
01:11:39,929 --> 01:11:41,468
- It'll be delicious. - It's going to be delicious.

1925
01:11:43,068 --> 01:11:45,167
Si Hyeon, you should...

1926
01:11:45,168 --> 01:11:46,367
(Prepping ingredients in earnest)

1927
01:11:46,368 --> 01:11:47,638
- cut these. - Okay.

1928
01:11:48,508 --> 01:11:50,208
- Sea cucumber. - That looks delicious.

1929
01:11:51,208 --> 01:11:52,338
I'll prep one for you.

1930
01:11:52,778 --> 01:11:54,377
Do it like this.

1931
01:11:54,378 --> 01:11:55,378
(Focused)

1932
01:11:56,378 --> 01:11:59,418
(Unlike earlier when they were filled with laughter,)

1933
01:12:01,188 --> 01:12:02,317
(it's gotten more serious.)

1934
01:12:02,318 --> 01:12:03,357
Remove the innards.

1935
01:12:03,358 --> 01:12:05,558
(It's gotten more serious.)

1936
01:12:06,958 --> 01:12:09,298
It's different from learning from a chef in Seoul...

1937
01:12:09,428 --> 01:12:11,558
- and from him. - Of course.

1938
01:12:12,258 --> 01:12:13,598
It's a real-life lesson.

1939
01:12:14,498 --> 01:12:17,068
As for the local dishes,

1940
01:12:17,438 --> 01:12:19,368
there are so many things...

1941
01:12:19,708 --> 01:12:22,137
that professional chefs don't know of.

1942
01:12:22,138 --> 01:12:23,278
That's what I realized.

1943
01:12:23,778 --> 01:12:25,378
- Since it's a local cooking method. - That's right.

1944
01:12:26,108 --> 01:12:29,248
When you come to regions that deal with seafood mostly,

1945
01:12:29,678 --> 01:12:32,248
you get to learn methods that go beyond your imagination.

1946
01:12:32,518 --> 01:12:35,488
There are various and deeper methods...

1947
01:12:35,581 --> 01:12:37,121
in regions.

1948
01:12:39,058 --> 01:12:41,958
(I'll prep sea cucumbers this time.)

1949
01:12:43,198 --> 01:12:45,428
(Cutting without hesitation)

1950
01:12:46,628 --> 01:12:47,628
(Removing)

1951
01:12:48,068 --> 01:12:50,167
(Removing the innards skillfully)

1952
01:12:50,168 --> 01:12:51,568
