2051
01:16:31,758 --> 01:16:33,488
This much. Then mix it.

2052
01:16:38,028 --> 01:16:40,398
(You add water to that?)

2053
01:16:42,128 --> 01:16:44,398
- Was it good? - It was really good.

2054
01:16:44,944 --> 01:16:45,984
It looks delicious.

2055
01:16:46,268 --> 01:16:48,207
It's neither gukbap nor seasoned vegetables.

2056
01:16:48,208 --> 01:16:49,208
Exactly.

2057
01:16:49,209 --> 01:16:51,178
It's a strange dish. You can even mix rice in it.

2058
01:16:51,370 --> 01:16:53,910
It becomes more delicious because of the carbs from rice.

2059
01:16:54,508 --> 01:16:56,617
It must have the scents from both mountains and ocean.

2060
01:16:56,618 --> 01:16:58,318
Yes. That's why it's called seolchi soup.

2061
01:16:59,488 --> 01:17:00,518
- "To mix?" - Yes.

2062
01:17:00,748 --> 01:17:01,918
Siler divaricata tangpyeongchae.

2063
01:17:02,758 --> 01:17:04,918
What should you add for the base of its taste?

2064
01:17:05,458 --> 01:17:06,628
- The crabs. - The crabs.

2065
01:17:06,828 --> 01:17:08,558
Now, pick out the crab meat.

2066
01:17:10,228 --> 01:17:11,398
That's really delicious.

2067
01:17:12,358 --> 01:17:13,428
There's juice inside.

2068
01:17:13,798 --> 01:17:16,168
We're going to mix the vegetables with this last.

2069
01:17:16,438 --> 01:17:17,797
- Imagine how delicious it'd be. - It must be delicious.

2070
01:17:17,798 --> 01:17:19,168
Collect it separately.

2071
01:17:20,128 --> 01:17:22,738
We're going to mix the vegetables with this last.

2072
01:17:23,298 --> 01:17:24,236
It must be so good.

2073
01:17:24,938 --> 01:17:26,867
Goodness. We add hairy crabs...

2074
01:17:26,868 --> 01:17:29,637
and the umami-rich crab juice.

2075
01:17:29,638 --> 01:17:31,337
Gosh, it must be delicious.

2076
01:17:31,338 --> 01:17:33,148
(Mixing with crab meat and innards)

2077
01:17:33,248 --> 01:17:35,508
To this, we'll add...

2078
01:17:35,978 --> 01:17:38,048
the shrimp and clams we prepared.

2079
01:17:39,518 --> 01:17:40,887
(The clams, shrimp, and oysters they stir-fried in advance)

2080
01:17:40,888 --> 01:17:44,288
So many ingredients and so much effort are added.

2081
01:17:45,318 --> 01:17:46,628
Add about this much.

2082
01:17:47,388 --> 01:17:48,588
Did they imagine...

2083
01:17:49,198 --> 01:17:50,957
they'd meet like that when they were alive?

2084
01:17:50,958 --> 01:17:53,168
- They'd never run into each other. - They must've had no idea.

2085
01:17:53,498 --> 01:17:56,238
Then add a bit of sesame oil.

2086
01:17:56,998 --> 01:17:59,038
You wouldn't be able to find this on a delivery app.

2087
01:18:01,438 --> 01:18:03,608
- I should visit Tongyeong. - The plating is nice.

2088
01:18:04,008 --> 01:18:05,907
I'm grateful that you showed this to us.

2089
01:18:05,908 --> 01:18:07,507
I wouldn't have known this dish until I died...

2090
01:18:07,508 --> 01:18:08,508
if you hadn't shown it to us.

2091
01:18:08,878 --> 01:18:10,418
- We'd have never known. - Right?

2092
01:18:11,278 --> 01:18:13,118
- Did you make them deliciously? - Yes.

2093
01:18:13,518 --> 01:18:14,547
Can I taste it?

2094
01:18:14,548 --> 01:18:15,548
- Yes, try that. - Of course.

2095
01:18:16,158 --> 01:18:17,958
You should have it with the soup.

2096
01:18:18,658 --> 01:18:20,388
(Taking a bite)

2097
01:18:20,658 --> 01:18:22,057
(How is it?)

2098
01:18:22,058 --> 01:18:23,058
Is it good?

2099
01:18:24,828 --> 01:18:25,898
Bring me rice.

2100
01:18:26,898 --> 01:18:27,927
"Bring me rice."

2101
01:18:27,928 --> 01:18:29,238
(Laughing)

2102
01:18:29,698 --> 01:18:31,168
- That's the best compliment. - You're right.

2103
01:18:32,138 --> 01:18:33,368
It's so good.

2104
01:18:33,468 --> 01:18:35,067
- I can't imagine its taste. - It's really good.

2105
01:18:35,068 --> 01:18:37,177
- How does it taste? - It is hard to imagine.

2106
01:18:37,178 --> 01:18:39,707
- It's a little hard to describe. - What does it taste like?

2107
01:18:39,708 --> 01:18:42,877
When they hold ancestral rites in Gyeongsang Province,

2108
01:18:42,878 --> 01:18:44,047
they serve radish soup.

2109
01:18:44,048 --> 01:18:45,917
- It has shrimp, clams, squid, - That's right.

2110
01:18:45,918 --> 01:18:48,548
and all sorts of seafood. There's radish soup like that.

2111
01:18:48,788 --> 01:18:51,317
They also serve seasoned seaweed.

2112
01:18:51,318 --> 01:18:53,288
You add all of them with rice.

2113
01:18:53,388 --> 01:18:54,757
Oh, that's how it tastes?

2114
01:18:54,758 --> 01:18:57,097
You can taste the radish from the radish soup...

2115
01:18:57,098 --> 01:18:59,297
and seasoned seaweed as well.

2116
01:18:59,298 --> 01:19:00,867
And the base is the radish soup?

2117
01:19:00,868 --> 01:19:02,497
- The base taste? - That's the taste.

2118
01:19:02,498 --> 01:19:04,338
It tastes like the soup from radish soup.

2119
01:19:04,498 --> 01:19:06,107
The taste from seafood radish soup...

2120
01:19:06,108 --> 01:19:07,937
- It's a little salty and... - Right? It's hard, right?

2121
01:19:07,938 --> 01:19:10,138
- I mean, I can't... - Their expressions were like...

2122
01:19:11,178 --> 01:19:12,948
It's hard to imagine for a man from Mokpo.

2123
01:19:13,378 --> 01:19:15,077
Oh, you don't hold ancestral rites?

2124
01:19:15,078 --> 01:19:16,478
It's hard for a man from Mokpo.

2125
01:19:17,448 --> 01:19:18,548
What's radish soup again?

2126
01:19:18,778 --> 01:19:19,888
You've never had radish soup?

2127
01:19:20,018 --> 01:19:21,688
- Radish soup... - You sure you're from Gyeongsang?

2128
01:19:22,548 --> 01:19:23,888
- I go to church, that's why. - People from there...

2129
01:19:26,558 --> 01:19:28,227
You only acted like you're from Busan.

2130
01:19:28,228 --> 01:19:29,557
(Joking)

2131
01:19:29,558 --> 01:19:30,897
I did live there.

2132
01:19:30,898 --> 01:19:32,327
You're a savvy Seoulite.

2133
01:19:32,328 --> 01:19:34,028
(It turns out he's a savvy Seoulite.)

2134
01:19:35,098 --> 01:19:37,297
Try the sea cucumber too. That's it.

2135
01:19:37,298 --> 01:19:39,138
(Trying a bite of siler divaricata tangpyeongchae as well)

2136
01:19:40,368 --> 01:19:41,938
- Siler divaricata is really sweet. - Its aroma is different.

2137
01:19:42,368 --> 01:19:43,907
You can actually sell this.

2138
01:19:43,908 --> 01:19:45,138
Yes. This is really good.

2139
01:19:45,308 --> 01:19:47,577
She got both compliments. "You can actually sell this."

2140
01:19:47,578 --> 01:19:49,747
- It's so good. - I'm going to Dongporu later.

2141
01:19:49,748 --> 01:19:50,878
- Are you? - Yes.

2142
01:19:51,348 --> 01:19:53,047
- Take this too. - I'll take this as well.

2143
01:19:53,048 --> 01:19:54,188
Then I will...

2144
01:19:54,318 --> 01:19:56,088
- It's perfect for eating alone. - It is.

2145
01:19:58,288 --> 01:20:00,088
(Taking her notebook out)

2146
01:20:00,458 --> 01:20:02,728
(She took out her notebook, seizing the chance.)

2147
01:20:03,458 --> 01:20:05,097
So it doesn't matter whatever ingredient I add...

2148
01:20:05,098 --> 01:20:06,767
to siler divaricata tangpyeongchae?

2149
01:20:06,768 --> 01:20:08,327
Yes, it doesn't have to be those seafood.

2150
01:20:08,328 --> 01:20:09,938
If you don't have hairy crabs,

2151
01:20:10,138 --> 01:20:11,298
you can add blue crabs.

2152
01:20:11,438 --> 01:20:14,308
You don't need to add sea cucumbers or crabs.

2153
01:20:14,768 --> 01:20:16,677
- Sea cucumbers are amazing, though. - The master...

2154
01:20:16,678 --> 01:20:18,878
is passing on all his knowledge.

2155
01:20:20,378 --> 01:20:22,008
How else do you eat sea cucumbers?

2156
01:20:22,718 --> 01:20:25,048
We used raw seaweed earlier after rinsing it, right?

2157
01:20:25,078 --> 01:20:26,387
Yes, stone seaweed.

2158
01:20:26,388 --> 01:20:27,787
(Her notes fill up a page in no time.)

2159
01:20:27,788 --> 01:20:28,988
That's a true asset.

2160
01:20:29,558 --> 01:20:32,158
Si Hyeon, I think you'll do well.

2161
01:20:32,728 --> 01:20:33,728
Thank you.

2162
01:20:33,988 --> 01:20:36,027
When I saw you mixing vegetables earlier,

2163
01:20:36,028 --> 01:20:37,258
I noticed that you could do it.

2164
01:20:37,598 --> 01:20:40,328
Some people mix them too hard.

2165
01:20:40,528 --> 01:20:43,968
It's just that you find whatever Si Hyeon does adorable.

2166
01:20:44,868 --> 01:20:46,868
You're not satisfied with whatever others do.

2167
01:20:47,338 --> 01:20:48,867
This is why I like coming to Tongyeong.

2168
01:20:48,868 --> 01:20:50,108
Is that so?

2169
01:20:50,238 --> 01:20:51,278
I agree.

2170
01:20:54,148 --> 01:20:57,018
The master dyed the wrapping cloth himself.

2171
01:20:57,078 --> 01:20:58,148
It's so pretty.

2172
01:21:00,688 --> 01:21:01,718
- Go on. - All right.

2173
01:21:02,418 --> 01:21:03,487
Let me hug you one last time.

2174
01:21:03,488 --> 01:21:06,488
(Let me hug you one last time, Si Hyeon.)

2175
01:21:07,128 --> 01:21:08,527
- Work hard, okay? - Okay.

2176
01:21:08,528 --> 01:21:10,558
- Don't lose your original spirit. - Studying is the only way.

2177
01:21:11,558 --> 01:21:14,228
(Okay!)

2178
01:21:14,968 --> 01:21:16,537
- Thank you. - Sure.

2179
01:21:16,538 --> 01:21:17,868
Thank you for this.

2180
01:21:19,038 --> 01:21:20,607
Her clip keeps feeling like a comic.

2181
01:21:20,608 --> 01:21:22,138
- I know. It does to me too. - Really?

2182
01:21:22,538 --> 01:21:23,607
You're like a real family.

2183
01:21:23,608 --> 01:21:24,638
Of course.

2184
01:21:28,178 --> 01:21:31,548
(She left after saying goodbye to her master sadly.)

2185
01:21:32,548 --> 01:21:36,558
(She trudges along somewhere like she's used to.)

2186
01:21:37,088 --> 01:21:39,488
Hello. I'd like it to go, please.

2187
01:21:40,428 --> 01:21:41,457
(She buys Chungmu gimbap as a takeaway order.)

2188
01:21:41,458 --> 01:21:42,587
- She got Chungmu gimbap. - Thank you.

2189
01:21:42,588 --> 01:21:43,727
That's my favorite place.

2190
01:21:43,728 --> 01:21:44,828
Have a good day.

2191
01:21:45,628 --> 01:21:47,667
(Then she sets off busily.)

2192
01:21:47,668 --> 01:21:49,328
- You must be eating it somewhere. - That's right.

2193
01:21:50,498 --> 01:21:52,868
(Gazing)

2194
01:21:54,168 --> 01:21:55,668
The weather was amazing.

2195
01:21:58,278 --> 01:21:59,848
You must be eating it on the turtle ship.

2196
01:22:05,878 --> 01:22:08,488
(Instead of the turtle ship, she sits on the bench in front.)

2197
01:22:08,718 --> 01:22:11,088
(Taking something out)

2198
01:22:13,458 --> 01:22:14,827
(She took out ice cream to recharge with sugar.)

2199
01:22:14,828 --> 01:22:15,858
I'm low on sugar.

2200
01:22:17,628 --> 01:22:19,498
(Taking a big scoop)

2201
01:22:19,798 --> 01:22:20,867
(Eating)

2202
01:22:20,868 --> 01:22:22,027
That must be good.

2203
01:22:22,028 --> 01:22:23,098
It was really good.

2204
01:22:26,808 --> 01:22:27,867
Oh, it's mochi.

2205
01:22:27,868 --> 01:22:30,208
(Mouth filled with chewiness)

2206
01:22:30,778 --> 01:22:32,078
The mochi is crazy delicious.

2207
01:22:33,778 --> 01:22:35,348
(Taking another bite)

2208
01:22:35,508 --> 01:22:36,778
Eating something sweet really hits the spot.

2209
01:22:38,548 --> 01:22:40,118
I was really low on sugar then.

2210
01:22:40,248 --> 01:22:41,718
(Finding her cute)

2211
01:22:44,418 --> 01:22:47,458
(Putting the empty cup back into the plastic bag)

2212
01:22:48,888 --> 01:22:51,228
(Let's go.)

2213
01:22:52,928 --> 01:22:55,597
(Setting off again now that she's refuelled with sugar)

2214
01:22:55,598 --> 01:22:57,238
The weather is amazing.

2215
01:22:58,838 --> 01:23:00,707
(Charming alleyway, Dongpirang)

2216
01:23:00,708 --> 01:23:01,868
Wait. It's Dongpirang.

2217
01:23:04,178 --> 01:23:05,508
It looks like a duck.

2218
01:23:07,548 --> 01:23:10,078
(The place she hurriedly got to)

2219
01:23:10,948 --> 01:23:12,018
Dongporu?

2220
01:23:13,688 --> 01:23:15,187
- Dongporu is... - It's pretty!

2221
01:23:15,188 --> 01:23:18,318
a gazebo on top of Dongpirang.

2222
01:23:18,558 --> 01:23:21,658
You can see the whole Tongyeong at once there.

2223
01:23:21,688 --> 01:23:25,658
I like the view that helps you clear your mind,

2224
01:23:26,128 --> 01:23:27,968
the pleasant wind,

2225
01:23:28,128 --> 01:23:31,268
and the quietness of the gazebo.

2226
01:23:31,568 --> 01:23:34,338
I always stop by Dongporu when the weather is nice.

2227
01:23:34,708 --> 01:23:36,678
(She takes out Chungmu gimbap as soon as she arrives.)

2228
01:23:37,608 --> 01:23:38,937
It's really simple, but it's delicious.

2229
01:23:38,938 --> 01:23:40,007
- I know. - It's really good.

2230
01:23:40,008 --> 01:23:41,107
It's only good when you eat it there.

2231
01:23:41,108 --> 01:23:43,347
- That's right. - From what I know,

2232
01:23:43,348 --> 01:23:44,417
Chungmu gimbap is what sailors ate...

2233
01:23:44,418 --> 01:23:46,148
- That's right. - because it wouldn't be spoiled.

2234
01:23:46,448 --> 01:23:47,717
That's what they chose.

2235
01:23:47,718 --> 01:23:49,147
Doesn't gimbap go bad really fast when it's outside?

2236
01:23:49,148 --> 01:23:50,517
- It doesn't have pickled radish. - That's right.

2237
01:23:50,518 --> 01:23:51,717
- Chungmu gimbap doesn't have it. - It has only rice and...

2238
01:23:51,718 --> 01:23:53,357
Oh, it's the filling that goes bad.

2239
01:23:53,358 --> 01:23:55,287
It's like fast food for sailors.

2240
01:23:55,288 --> 01:23:56,327
(I see.)

2241
01:23:56,328 --> 01:23:58,257
It has only rice and seasoned squid on the side.

2242
01:23:58,258 --> 01:23:59,797
I'm learning a lot today.

2243
01:23:59,798 --> 01:24:01,298
(This is fun.)

2244
01:24:02,168 --> 01:24:05,298
(She's done setting everything up to eat conveniently.)

2245
01:24:06,338 --> 01:24:08,668
- Gosh. - Gosh, it's driving me crazy.

2246
01:24:09,268 --> 01:24:10,707
- It looks so good. - I must go to Tongyeong.

2247
01:24:10,708 --> 01:24:12,037
(Siler divaricata tangpyeongchae and seolchi soup...)

2248
01:24:12,038 --> 01:24:13,378
(that resembles Tongyeong's nature)

2249
01:24:15,048 --> 01:24:16,178
They look so good.

2250
01:24:17,148 --> 01:24:19,618
(Grabbing seolchi soup first)

2251
01:24:23,218 --> 01:24:24,958
(It's indeed good.)

2252
01:24:29,128 --> 01:24:30,758
I should have this soup on my birthday.

2253
01:24:31,058 --> 01:24:33,198
It feels strange to see her eat with that flag.

2254
01:24:34,328 --> 01:24:35,698
It looks like I conquered the city.

2255
01:24:36,368 --> 01:24:38,567
- Like a general's daughter. - She took over Tongyeong.

2256
01:24:38,568 --> 01:24:39,808
(The baby general who conquered Tongyeong's seasoned vegetables)

2257
01:24:41,008 --> 01:24:45,278
(This time, she takes a bite to take over Chungmu gimbap.)

2258
01:24:49,748 --> 01:24:51,817
(She takes a bite of spicy seokbakji right away.)

2259
01:24:51,818 --> 01:24:54,247
- That must be good. - It really is good. Gosh.

2260
01:24:54,248 --> 01:24:55,418
That's really good.

2261
01:24:55,918 --> 01:24:58,088
(Staring)

2262
01:24:59,188 --> 01:25:01,227
The view is to die for.

2263
01:25:01,228 --> 01:25:02,488
The view is amazing too.

2264
01:25:04,728 --> 01:25:07,067
(She eats up siler divaricata tangpyeongchae...)

2265
01:25:07,068 --> 01:25:09,468
(after seeing the ocean.)

2266
01:25:10,438 --> 01:25:11,637
(Then she stares at the ocean again.)

2267
01:25:11,638 --> 01:25:13,308
Gosh, it's lovely.

2268
01:25:13,338 --> 01:25:14,368
Gosh.

2269
01:25:16,378 --> 01:25:18,878
I'm so serious about Tongyeong, and I go there so often.

2270
01:25:19,078 --> 01:25:22,608
People around me call me the daughter of Tongyeong too.

2271
01:25:22,778 --> 01:25:23,948
That's how much I love Tongyeong.

2272
01:25:24,048 --> 01:25:25,447
It helped me clear my mind,

2273
01:25:25,448 --> 01:25:28,818
and I got to smell the vegetables and pick them happily.

2274
01:25:28,988 --> 01:25:32,188
I felt rich after picking a basket of them.

2275
01:25:32,688 --> 01:25:34,158
It's like a haven for my heart.

2276
01:25:34,388 --> 01:25:37,158
I get no stress whenever I go to Tongyeong,

2277
01:25:37,398 --> 01:25:38,758
and I become relaxed.

2278
01:25:39,158 --> 01:25:41,768
It's like a hometown I go to whenever I'm struggling.

2279
01:25:44,138 --> 01:25:46,938
Siler divaricata is a bit bitter,

2280
01:25:47,608 --> 01:25:49,837
but the sea cucumber's sweetness dialed it down.

2281
01:25:49,838 --> 01:25:51,178
- You constantly study. - Yes.

2282
01:25:52,778 --> 01:25:58,748
(Returned to the Home of My Heart)

2283
01:25:58,848 --> 01:26:00,348
(Next story)

2284
01:26:00,888 --> 01:26:01,918
(Clicking)

2285
01:26:02,718 --> 01:26:03,858
(Wilson is here.)

2286
01:26:03,918 --> 01:26:05,458
(Wilson is here.)

2287
01:26:08,288 --> 01:26:09,457
(She's been living alone for 14 years.)

2288
01:26:09,458 --> 01:26:10,558
(It's Comedian Kim Shin Young.)

2289
01:26:12,128 --> 01:26:13,468
(Welcome to Shin Young's world.)

2290
01:26:14,628 --> 01:26:16,068
(The maximalist's taste is reflected here and there.)

2291
01:26:16,468 --> 01:26:17,767
(A denim room)

2292
01:26:17,768 --> 01:26:18,768
(And a shoes room)

2293
01:26:19,468 --> 01:26:21,238
(There's even a dressing room that looks like a maze.)

2294
01:26:22,038 --> 01:26:23,838
(If I sell them all, I can buy this place.)

2295
01:26:27,348 --> 01:26:28,678
(Heading straight to the rice cooker as soon as she gets up?)

2296
01:26:29,778 --> 01:26:32,018
(In the morning, she has the peak appetite.)

2297
01:26:33,418 --> 01:26:35,088
(She starts with slurping noodles.)

2298
01:26:36,318 --> 01:26:38,918
(A perfectly customized meal course for herself)

2299
01:26:39,888 --> 01:26:42,458
(Wrapping up with seaweed tea for her health)

2300
01:26:43,098 --> 01:26:44,098
(Gosh, this is nice.)

2301
01:26:44,858 --> 01:26:46,828
(An extreme homebody's routine)

2302
01:26:47,298 --> 01:26:48,628
(Why wouldn't it work?)

2303
01:26:49,628 --> 01:26:51,398
(I have so much to do today!)

2304
01:26:51,568 --> 01:26:52,598
Goodness.

2305
01:26:53,208 --> 01:26:54,468
(An alarm rang!)

2306
01:26:55,668 --> 01:26:58,708
(Since she needs to fill her off-day with happiness...)

2307
01:27:00,308 --> 01:27:01,348
This is perfect.

2308
01:27:02,348 --> 01:27:03,978
(The last alarm of the day comes from her stomach.)

2309
01:27:05,048 --> 01:27:06,947
(Perfect timing)

2310
01:27:06,948 --> 01:27:08,718
(Perfect seasoning)

2311
01:27:09,958 --> 01:27:12,717
(A Perfect Day)

2312
01:27:12,718 --> 01:27:15,028
(An Almost Perfect Day)

2313
01:27:15,488 --> 01:27:16,898
(Neat outfit, neat hair)

2314
01:27:17,198 --> 01:27:19,228
(And a mysteriously big bag?)

2315
01:27:19,458 --> 01:27:21,428
(Woo Il is heading somewhere excitedly.)

2316
01:27:21,868 --> 01:27:22,898
(Today is an especially important day.)

2317
01:27:23,238 --> 01:27:25,398
(Where did Woo Il who dressed up extra nice head to?)

2318
01:27:27,168 --> 01:27:29,668
(It's a cooking class he's been going to frequently recently.)

2319
01:27:30,338 --> 01:27:32,378
(He got through the past days with simple meals.)

2320
01:27:33,448 --> 01:27:35,208
(Investing in today's meal and future jobs)

2321
01:27:36,408 --> 01:27:38,547
(He's been working hard constantly...)

2322
01:27:38,548 --> 01:27:41,388
(for a long time.)

2323
01:27:42,018 --> 01:27:44,758
(Seriously passionate without trying to be funny)

2324
01:27:45,018 --> 01:27:46,588
(Why did you soak the potatoes in water?)

2325
01:27:47,088 --> 01:27:48,858
(Passion for learning boiling over)

2326
01:27:49,528 --> 01:27:51,758
(Confidence built up step by step)

2327
01:27:52,458 --> 01:27:53,798
(Let's go for it again today.)

2328
01:27:54,628 --> 01:27:56,268
(Cut the cartilage only.)

2329
01:27:56,968 --> 01:27:58,768
(Like this?)

2330
01:27:59,538 --> 01:28:01,107
(I don't think it has cartilage.)

2331
01:28:01,108 --> 01:28:02,608
(Yes, it does.)

2332
01:28:02,777 --> 01:28:03,777
(Embarrassed)

2333
01:28:03,802 --> 01:28:05,077
(Please prepare starch water.)

2334
01:28:05,078 --> 01:28:06,138
(Grease it again.)

2335
01:28:06,508 --> 01:28:07,878
(Flustering about due to a series of missions)

2336
01:28:08,578 --> 01:28:10,278
(Please wrap it up in 10 minutes.)

2337
01:28:11,548 --> 01:28:13,018
(On top of everything, he's pressed for time.)

2338
01:28:13,518 --> 01:28:14,818
(Let's hurry up.)

2339
01:28:15,288 --> 01:28:16,758
(A huge mistake)

2340
01:28:17,288 --> 01:28:18,318
(What's wrong with me today?)

2341
01:28:19,488 --> 01:28:24,398
(Nothing Seems to be Easy)
